{"id":"assistant-7cbf018a-8244-5402-9997-cfaba1a3b9b6","sessionId":"31e0a13f-33ae-d5ff-5a35-296c14ef1dec","turnId":"turn-2571d696126a52b8b736c18455fd86f5","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2571d696126a52b8b736c18455fd86f5-1","createdAt":1794285315645,"updatedAt":1794285315645,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! Now let me write the ANSWER.md file explaining the change:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
{"id":"effect-f63f739a-b639-58e1-ac1a-7eaeb48327b9","sessionId":"31e0a13f-33ae-d5ff-5a35-296c14ef1dec","turnId":"turn-2571d696126a52b8b736c18455fd86f5","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2571d696126a52b8b736c18455fd86f5-1","createdAt":1794285315649,"updatedAt":1794285315657,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for System Prompt Caching with Long-Term Memory\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was causing the entire system prompt to be reprocessed at full price, as seen in `logs/usage.jsonl` where `cache_creation_input_tokens` spikes after each memory write.\n\nThe root cause: `build_system()` was concatenating the static `INSTRUCTIONS` with the dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single system message block. When `save_fact` modified `a.facts`, the `athlete_context` changed, which changed the entire system prompt text, causing a cache miss for the static instructions.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate blocks in `build_system()`:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - passed as a plain text block without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached with a stable key\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - passed with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, explicitly marked as non-cacheable\n\nThis way, the static instructions (which never change) maintain a stable cache key, while the athlete-specific context (which changes with `save_fact`) is explicitly ephemeral and doesn't evict the static portion from cache.\n\n## Change Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n```python\n# Before:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n\n# After:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\nThe static `INSTRUCTIONS` block now has no `cache_control`, so it gets a stable cache key based on its content. The dynamic `athlete_context` block is explicitly ephemeral and won't affect the caching of the static instructions.\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for System Prompt Caching with Long-Term Memory\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was causing the entire system prompt to be reprocessed at full price, as seen in `logs/usage.jsonl` where `cache_creation_input_tokens` spikes after each memory write.\n\nThe root cause: `build_system()` was concatenating the static `INSTRUCTIONS` with the dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single system message block. When `save_fact` modified `a.facts`, the `athlete_context` changed, which changed the entire system prompt text, causing a cache miss for the static instructions.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate blocks in `build_system()`:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - passed as a plain text block without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached with a stable key\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - passed with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, explicitly marked as non-cacheable\n\nThis way, the static instructions (which never change) maintain a stable cache key, while the athlete-specific context (which changes with `save_fact`) is explicitly ephemeral and doesn't evict the static portion from cache.\n\n## Change Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n```python\n# Before:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n\n# After:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\nThe static `INSTRUCTIONS` block now has no `cache_control`, so it gets a stable cache key based on its content. The dynamic `athlete_context` block is explicitly ephemeral and won't affect the caching of the static instructions.\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","approvalType":"always","durationMs":0.0,"approvalSource":"bypass","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-tVNOAA/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for System Prompt Caching with Long-Term Memory\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was causing the entire system prompt to be reprocessed at full price, as seen in `logs/usage.jsonl` where `cache_creation_input_tokens` spikes after each memory write.\n\nThe root cause: `build_system()` was concatenating the static `INSTRUCTIONS` with the dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single system message block. When `save_fact` modified `a.facts`, the `athlete_context` changed, which changed the entire system prompt text, causing a cache miss for the static instructions.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate blocks in `build_system()`:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - passed as a plain text block without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached with a stable key\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - passed with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, explicitly marked as non-cacheable\n\nThis way, the static instructions (which never change) maintain a stable cache key, while the athlete-specific context (which changes with `save_fact`) is explicitly ephemeral and doesn't evict the static portion from cache.\n\n## Change Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n```python\n# Before:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \"\\n\\n\" + athlete_context(a, today)\n    return [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": text, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}]\n\n# After:\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\nThe static `INSTRUCTIONS` block now has no `cache_control`, so it gets a stable cache key based on its content. The dynamic `athlete_context` block is explicitly ephemeral and won't affect the caching of the static instructions.\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null},"display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"decision":"execute"}}
