{"id":"assistant-e16a487b-06e3-5fa4-a64d-29c668c3d64b","sessionId":"31e0a13f-33ae-d5ff-5a35-296c14ef1dec","turnId":"turn-2571d696126a52b8b736c18455fd86f5","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2571d696126a52b8b736c18455fd86f5-1","createdAt":1794285373961,"updatedAt":1794285373961,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All tests pass. Let me create a final summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue in the bot. Here's what was done:\n\n### Problem Identified\nThe `build_system()` function was concatenating the static `INSTRUCTIONS` with the dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single system message block. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, causing a cache miss and requiring the full system prompt (including the static instructions) to be reprocessed at full token cost.\n\n### Solution Implemented\nModified the `build_system()` function in `bot.py` to split the system prompt into two separate blocks:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS block** - No `cache_control` attribute, allowing it to be cached with a stable key based on its content\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context block** - Explicitly marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, so it's not cached\n\n### Changes Made\n- **File modified**: `bot.py` - Updated the `build_system()` function (lines 130-137)\n- **File created**: `ANSWER.md` - Documentation of the fix\n\n### Verification\n- Syntax check: ✓ Python code compiles without errors\n- Unit tests: ✓ All three comprehensive tests pass\n- Integration: ✓ The `build_request()` function correctly uses the new system format\n- Cache behavior: ✓ First block (INSTRUCTIONS) remains stable when facts change; second block (athlete_context) changes as expected\n\nThe fix ensures that `save_fact` calls no longer evict the static instructions from the cache, reducing token usage for subsequent requests."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
